 direction, starting from $(r+a,b).$\n\nIn our case, we have a circle of radius $3$ centered at the point $(3,-2).$ Therefore, the parametric equations of the circle are\n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +3,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -2,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997706/state.json" "file_sha256" "be160248e907dc0090c0e85ac5f1243f82e74a4127fd354d2039dad9e67a4fd7" "basis" 1075 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997706/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-106291" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997706/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e404b38bbdf5c756f675cf0dfcc2c4906bcd2d62b1b4d277b8fc0cfb85e9b2d4" "basis" 1075 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997706/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-106291" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997706/state.json" "file_sha256" "be160248e907dc0090c0e85ac5f1243f82e74a4127fd354d2039dad9e67a4fd7" "basis" 1075 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997706/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-106291" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=12\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -4,\\,y=12\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +6"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997706/state.json" "file_sha256" "be160248e907dc0090c0e85ac5f1243f82e74a4127fd354d2039dad9e67a4fd7" "basis" 1075 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Co